    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok i get the rainbow table part, but i'm still a bit confused on how it actually works during the process. like, where does the salt go? is it added before or after the password gets hashed? and is the salt itself kept secret or stored in the database with the user?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The salt is generated randomly for each user and added to the password string **before** the password is hashed. This combined value (salt + password) is then passed into the hashing function to create the unique password hash. Crucially, the salt itself is **not secret**; it is always stored in the database alongside the password so that an attacker who gains database access can still generate all possible salted combinations to attempt to crack the hash during an offline brute force attack. Without storing the salt, the system would be unable to independently verify the password during login.",
